'''absorbability''' (ạb-sôr-bạ-bil′i-ti), ''n.'' The state or quality of being absorbable.

'''absorbable''' (ạb-sôr′bạ-bl), ''a.'' Capable of being absorbed or imbibed.

'''absorbed''' (ạb-sôrbd′), ''p. a.'' 1. Drawn in or sucked up. {{smaller|Specifically applied to the coloring in paintings when the oil has sunk into the canvas, leaving the color flat and the touches dead or indistinct: nearly synonymous with ''sunk in''.}}

2. Engrossed: as, an ''absorbed'' look.

'''absorbedly''' (ạb-sôr′bed-li), ''adv.'' In an absorbed manner.

